<title>USA: Excel Corp shutting Ill hog plant for maintenance.</title>
<headline>Excel Corp shutting Ill hog plant for maintenance.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Excel Corp confirmed early Thursday it was shutting its hog slaughter and processing plant in Beardstown, Ill., Friday through Monday for planned maintenance.</p>
<p>The maintenance will include a scheduled upgrade of the plant's refrigeration units, said Mark Klein, Excel spokesman.</p>
<p>Trade estimates put the plant's daily slaughter capacity at about 16,000 head.  </p>
<p>&quot;This has been planned for several months,&quot; Klein said.</p>
<p>Excel Corp is a division of  Cargill Inc. Excel also operates hog plants in Ottumwa, Iowa and Marshall, Mo.</p>
<p>	  ((Bob Janis 312-983-7347))</p>
